          </h2>

          <p>
            Most hand vacuums are dry only. Using one on liquid can damage the motor and the filter.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What Counts as a Wet Mess</h3>

          <p>
            Spilled drinks, a pet's water bowl, a leak under the sink or melted snow at the door all need a wet-capable vacuum, or towels.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The Wet-Dry Option</h3>

          <p>
            The DEWALT DCV517B is built for wet and dry pick-up, with a half-gallon tank and a wet/dry HEPA filter. Empty and rinse the tank after wet jobs, and let the filter dry before the next dry clean.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Dry Hand Vacs and Damp Debris</h3>

          <p>
            Damp debris, like wet cereal or soil, can clog and smear inside a dry vac. Let it dry or wipe it up first, and never use a dry-only vac on liquid.
          </p>
        </div>

