            11. How Much Should You Spend on a Handheld Vacuum?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Hand vacuums cover a wide price range, and the extra money buys specific things rather than general quality.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Entry Level: Crumbs and Dry Spills</h3>

          <p>
            A basic dustbuster like the BLACK+DECKER AdvancedClean handles the everyday kitchen and entryway jobs well. If you have no pets and mostly hard floors, there is little reason to spend more.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Mid-Range: Pet Hair and Bigger Cups</h3>

          <p>
            Spending more buys a motorized or self-cleaning pet brush, a larger dust cup and stronger suction, as on the BLACK+DECKER furbuster and the Shark UltraCyclone. These are worth it for pet owners and homes with carpeted stairs.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Battery Platforms: Value Depends on What You Own</h3>

          <p>
            The DEWALT and Hoover ONEPWR models are good value if you already own their batteries, and expensive if you do not. Price the battery and charger in before comparing them with all-in-one models.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Vacuuming Liquids With a Dry Hand Vac</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Most hand vacuums are dry only, and liquid can damage the motor and ruin the filter. Use towels, or a wet/dry model like the DEWALT DCV517B. Even damp debris can clog and smear inside a dry vac.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Letting the Dust Cup Fill Up</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Suction drops sharply as the cup fills and the filter clogs. Empty after every use, especially with pet hair, which packs tightly and blocks airflow quickly.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Refitting a Wet Filter</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Washable filters need to dry completely before going back in. A damp filter grows mildew, smells and clogs faster. Wash it at night and refit it in the morning, or keep a spare.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying Suction Without a Brush for Pet Hair</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Suction alone struggles with hair woven into fabric. If pet hair on furniture is the main job, choose a model with a motorized or pet brush, like the Shark UltraCyclone or BLACK+DECKER furbuster.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a Bare-Tool Vac Without Checking the Battery</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The DEWALT DCV517B is sold without a battery or charger. It is good value if you already own DEWALT 20V MAX packs, but expensive if you have to buy them. Check what is in the box before you order any battery-platform tool.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

