            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best handheld vacuum for pet hair?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The Shark UltraCyclone Pet Pro Plus, for its self-cleaning Pet Power Brush and XL cup. On a budget, the BLACK+DECKER dustbuster furbuster has an anti-tangle motorized brush with rubber bristles, a 20V MAX battery and a POWERBOOST mode, per its listing. A motorized brush lifts hair from upholstery far better than suction alone.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the most powerful handheld vacuum?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Among household hand vacs here, the 20V models and Shark's cyclonic designs are the strongest options, but most makers do not publish comparable suction figures, so direct comparisons are difficult. For heavy-duty jobs, including wet spills, the DEWALT 20V MAX DCV517B wet/dry hand vacuum with its half-gallon tank is the most capable pick on this list.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are handheld vacuums worth it?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes, for most homes. A hand vac makes quick jobs quick: crumbs on the counter, pet hair on the sofa, dust on the stairs, litter by the box. Because it is light and always on charge, you use it in the moment rather than waiting for the weekly vacuum. Models like the BLACK+DECKER AdvancedClean are inexpensive.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is a dust buster?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Dustbuster is BLACK+DECKER's brand name for its handheld vacuums, and the word is now widely used for any small cordless hand vac. The BLACK+DECKER dustbuster AdvancedClean HLVA320J26 is the classic version, with a translucent washable dirt bowl, a pull-out crevice tool and a flip-up brush, per its listing.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a handheld vacuum pick up water?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Only if it is designed for wet pick-up. Most hand vacuums, including all the Shark and BLACK+DECKER models here, are dry only, and liquid can damage them. The DEWALT 20V MAX DCV517B is a wet/dry hand vacuum with a half-gallon tank and a wet/dry HEPA filter, built for spills.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long do handheld vacuum batteries last?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
